{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>My sister, daughter of my father.</b> Some say it is like 'the Elohim of my father Abraham' [i.e., a construct chain lacking the nomen regens], but the correct view in my eyes is that he fended off Avimelekh with words according to the need of the moment. And in the pericope of 'I am Esau your firstborn' (Genesis 27:19) I will bring the proofs."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:13.236973036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}